## 6. Population, perimeter, chamber-count, and Oler-slack propagation is valid

Canonical Sections 63/67 give

\[
m-R_4=(P_F+H_D)/2+1.
\]

Canonical Section 77 gives

\[
P_{ch}\ge J_D,
\qquad
s_{ch}=f+a\ge f.
\]

The exact chamber slack identity is

\[
\Sigma_{ch}
={A_{ch}-a_0Z_{ch}\over a_0}+{P_{ch}\over2}+s_{ch}.
\]

Since `A_ch-a0 Z_ch>=c0 H_D` and `c0/a0=1/2`, the candidate obtains

\[
\Sigma_{ch}\ge H_D/2+J_D/2+f
\ge4J_D/5+f.
\]

No internal chamber perimeter is cancelled or silently dropped.

**Verdict:** PASS.

## 7. The rhombus-count deficit follows from the full-source Oler bound

The full source obeys

\[
n\le\Delta_2D^2+\pi D/2+1.
\]

Since `m<=n` and

\[
\liminf(m-R_4)/D\ge\pi/2+3J_*/10,
